IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ntmaccc-dates`
IMPORT `ntmaccc-claims`

-- Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission Act 2014 (NT) -- worked cases for the questions of a person with a claim on
-- the Commission.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory; quoted under the NT
-- copyright policy of 8 October 1996 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). This is not an official version of the Act.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts and answers used below`

`OWN NAME` MEANS `the Commission, under its own name`
`TRADING NAME` MEANS `the Commission, under a business or trading name`
`COMMISSIONER` MEANS `the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner`
`PUBLIC SERVANT` MEANS `a Chief Executive Officer or a public sector employee`
`STAT CORP` MEANS `a statutory corporation`
`PRIVATE` MEANS `a private company or other non-government person`
`SUB` MEANS `someone to whom that private company or person passed the work on`

`A own` MEANS `yes: the Commission administers the MAC scheme under the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (s 7(a)), with all the powers of an individual (s 8); it is the Territory Insurance Office continued under a new name (s 5(1))`
`A name yes` MEANS `yes: the Commission may operate under a business or trading name the Minister has approved (s 11)`
`A name silent` MEANS `this Act does not say: s 11 lets the Commission use only names the Minister has approved, and says nothing of other names (NOTHING-kind)`
`A commissioner` MEANS `yes: the Commission is constituted by the Commissioner and any Associate Commissioners (s 5(3)(a)), and may delegate to them (s 9(1)(a))`
`A public yes` MEANS `yes: the Commission may delegate its powers and functions to a Chief Executive Officer, a public sector employee or a statutory corporation (s 9(1)(b), (c)), and has done so`
`A public silent` MEANS `this Act does not say: without a delegation from the Commission, s 9 gives them nothing (NOTHING-kind)`
`A sale` MEANS `yes: a non-government delegate under the contract made in the sale of TIO, which is taken to be a delegation contract (s 9(5))`
`A private yes` MEANS `yes: a non-government delegate, with the Minister's approval and a written delegation contract whose terms the Minister approved (s 9(1)(d), (2), (3))`
`A no approval` MEANS `no: a delegation to a non-government person needs the Minister's approval (s 9(1)(d), the text's no)`
`A no writing` MEANS `no: a delegation to a non-government person must be made by written contract (s 9(2), the text's no)`
`A no terms` MEANS `no: the Commission must not enter into a delegation contract unless the Minister has approved its terms (s 9(3), the text's no)`
`A sub yes` MEANS `yes: a sub-delegate of a non-government delegate, as the delegation contract permits (s 9(4)(a))`
`A sub no` MEANS `no: a non-government delegate may sub-delegate only if the delegation contract permits it (s 9(4)(a), the text's no)`

`who handles` MEANS `s 5, s 9, s 11 -- is the one handling my claim acting for the Commission`

§ `s 5, s 9, s 11 -- is the one handling my claim acting for the Commission`

-- Inputs, in order: who, name approved, delegated, made in the sale of TIO, Minister approved the delegation, written
-- contract, Minister approved the terms, sub-delegation permitted.
#ASSERT `who handles` `OWN NAME` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `A own`
#ASSERT `who handles` `TRADING NAME` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `A name yes`
#ASSERT `who handles` `TRADING NAME` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `A name silent`
#ASSERT `who handles` `COMMISSIONER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `A commissioner`
#ASSERT `who handles` `PUBLIC SERVANT` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `A public yes`
#ASSERT `who handles` `PUBLIC SERVANT` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `A public silent`
#ASSERT `who handles` `STAT CORP` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `A public yes`
#ASSERT `who handles` `STAT CORP` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `A public silent`
-- The claims company engaged in the sale of TIO: s 9(5) alone settles it, whatever the other answers.
#ASSERT `who handles` `PRIVATE` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `A sale`
#ASSERT `who handles` `PRIVATE` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `A sale`
-- A later contract: all three of s 9(1)(d), (2), (3) needed.
#ASSERT `who handles` `PRIVATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `A private yes`
#ASSERT `who handles` `PRIVATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `A no approval`
#ASSERT `who handles` `PRIVATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `A no writing`
#ASSERT `who handles` `PRIVATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `A no terms`
#ASSERT `who handles` `PRIVATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `A no approval`
-- Sub-delegates: the delegate's own standing first, then the contract's permission (s 9(4)(a)).
#ASSERT `who handles` `SUB` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `A sub yes`
#ASSERT `who handles` `SUB` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `A sub no`
#ASSERT `who handles` `SUB` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `A sub yes`
#ASSERT `who handles` `SUB` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `A sub no`
#ASSERT `who handles` `SUB` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `A no terms`
#ASSERT `who handles` `SUB` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `A no approval`
#ASSERT `who handles` `SUB` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `A no writing`

-- The helper on its own.
#ASSERT `a non-government delegate under s 9` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `a non-government delegate under s 9` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`a non-government delegate under s 9` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE))

§ `s 5(2)(c), s 15 -- can I hold them liable`

`L commission` MEANS `the Commission may be sued (s 5(2)(c)); s 15 does not affect any liability the Commission has (s 15(3)); whether it is liable is for the general law and the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (NOTHING-kind on liability)`
`L territory` MEANS `s 15 does not affect any liability the Territory has (s 15(3)), and the Territory guarantees the Commission's liabilities in the MAC business (s 27); beyond that, this Act does not say (NOTHING-kind on liability)`
`L s15(1)` MEANS `no: the Commissioner or Associate Commissioner is not civilly or criminally liable for an act or omission done in good faith in that role (s 15(1), the text's no); the Commission's and the Territory's liability is unaffected (s 15(3))`
`L s15(2)` MEANS `no: the Commissioner or Associate Commissioner is not civilly or criminally liable for an act or omission of the Commission, whether or not in good faith (s 15(2), the text's no); the Commission's and the Territory's liability is unaffected (s 15(3))`
`L bad faith` MEANS `this Act does not protect them: the act was not in good faith, so s 15(1) does not apply; whether they are liable is for the general law (NOTHING-kind)`
`L outside` MEANS `this Act does not say: s 15 protects only acts in the role of Commissioner or Associate Commissioner, or of the Commission (NOTHING-kind)`

`OWN ACT` MEANS `the Commissioner's or Associate Commissioner's own act or omission in exercising, or purporting to exercise, a power or function as Commissioner`
`COMMISSION ACT` MEANS `an act or omission of the Commission in exercising, or purporting to exercise, its powers or functions, including administering the MAC scheme`
`OUTSIDE` MEANS `something the Commissioner or Associate Commissioner did outside those roles`
`liable` MEANS `s 5(2)(c), s 15 -- can I hold them liable`

#ASSERT `liable` `the Commission` `OWN ACT` FALSE EQUALS `L commission`
#ASSERT `liable` `the Commission` `COMMISSION ACT` TRUE EQUALS `L commission`
#ASSERT `liable` `the Northern Territory` `COMMISSION ACT` FALSE EQUALS `L territory`
#ASSERT `liable` `the Northern Territory` `OUTSIDE` TRUE EQUALS `L territory`
#ASSERT `liable` `the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner personally` `OWN ACT` TRUE EQUALS `L s15(1)`
#ASSERT `liable` `the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner personally` `OWN ACT` FALSE EQUALS `L bad faith`
-- s 15(2) has no good-faith condition (finding 2): the answer is the same either way.
#ASSERT `liable` `the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner personally` `COMMISSION ACT` TRUE EQUALS `L s15(2)`
#ASSERT `liable` `the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner personally` `COMMISSION ACT` FALSE EQUALS `L s15(2)`
#ASSERT `liable` `the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner personally` `OUTSIDE` TRUE EQUALS `L outside`
#ASSERT `liable` `the Commissioner or an Associate Commissioner personally` `OUTSIDE` FALSE EQUALS `L outside`

§ `s 27 -- does the Territory guarantee what the Commission owes me`

`G yes` MEANS `yes: all liabilities of the Commission in relation to the MAC business are guaranteed by the Territory (s 27(1)), and amounts under the guarantee are paid from the Central Holding Authority (s 27(2))`
`G bank` MEANS `this Act gives that liability no guarantee: s 27 covers the MAC business only, and says nothing of the rest (NOTHING-kind); for the residual banking business, the moneys held for it are the Territory's property (s 34(1))`
`G none` MEANS `this Act gives that liability no guarantee: s 27 covers the MAC business, and says nothing of the rest (NOTHING-kind)`
`guarantee` MEANS `s 27 -- does the Territory guarantee what the Commission owes me`

#ASSERT `guarantee` `benefits or another liability under the MAC scheme or out of the Fund` EQUALS `G yes`
#ASSERT `guarantee` `a liability of TIO's insurance business that was not sold` EQUALS `G none`
#ASSERT `guarantee` `a deposit or other liability of TIO's banking business that was not sold` EQUALS `G bank`
#ASSERT `guarantee` `something else` EQUALS `G none`

§ `s 17(2) -- can it be paid out of the Fund`

`F yes` MEANS `yes: that is one of the purposes for which the Commission may pay amounts out of the Fund (s 17(2)); the Fund belongs to the Territory and is held by the Commission for it, not on trust (s 16(2), (3))`
`F no` MEANS `no: the Commission may pay amounts out of the Fund only for the purposes listed in s 17(2), and this is not one of them (the text's no)`
`fund` MEANS `s 17(2) -- can it be paid out of the Fund`

#ASSERT `fund` `benefits under the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979` EQUALS `F yes`
#ASSERT `fund` `the cost of administering the MAC scheme` EQUALS `F yes`
#ASSERT `fund` `the cost of managing the Fund` EQUALS `F yes`
#ASSERT `fund` `amounts the Commission owes under a contract delegating MAC work (a MAC management agreement)` EQUALS `F yes`
#ASSERT `fund` `another liability in relation to the MAC business` EQUALS `F yes`
#ASSERT `fund` `staff and facilities, reimbursing public health services, the prudential supervision fee, or a surplus paid to the Territory (s 14(3), 18, 19, 20)` EQUALS `F yes`
#ASSERT `fund` `promoting road safety` EQUALS `F yes`
#ASSERT `fund` `something else, such as a liability of TIO's former insurance or banking business` EQUALS `F no`

§ `s 18 -- is my public treatment reimbursed from the Fund`

`H yes` MEANS `yes: you are a MAC claimant and these are public health services, so their cost is among what the Minister must consider reimbursing to the Territory after the financial year, in the amount (if any) the Minister determines (s 18(1)); the Commission pays it out of the Fund within 2 months after the Minister's notice (s 18(2)); this Act does not say whether you are charged (NOTHING-kind)`
`H not claimant` MEANS `no: you are not a MAC claimant, a person entitled to compensation under s 18 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (s 18(3), the text's no)`
`H not medical` MEANS `no: only medical and rehabilitation services count as public health services (s 18(3), the text's no)`
`H not public` MEANS `no: only services provided by NT Regional Health Services count as public health services (s 18(3), the text's no); a private provider's charges fall under s 18 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 itself`
`H not compensable` MEANS `no: the services would not have been compensable under s 18 of the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 had a private provider given them, so they are not public health services (s 18(3), the text's no)`
`health` MEANS `s 18 -- is my public treatment reimbursed from the Fund`

-- Inputs: entitled under s 18 of the MAC Act, medical or rehabilitation, by NT Regional Health Services, compensable if
-- private.
#ASSERT `health` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `H yes`
#ASSERT `health` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `H not claimant`
#ASSERT `health` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `H not claimant`
#ASSERT `health` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `H not medical`
#ASSERT `health` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `H not public`
#ASSERT `health` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `H not compensable`
#ASSERT `health` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `H not public`

§ `s 28 -- was disclosing my information an offence`

`D not obtained` MEANS `no: s 28 does not reach it, since the person did not obtain the information in performing functions connected with the administration of this Act (s 28(1)(a), the text's no)`
`D none` MEANS `no: nothing was disclosed (s 28(1)(b), the text's no)`
`D excepted` MEANS `no: s 28(1) does not apply to a disclosure for the administration of this Act, with your consent, for legal proceedings arising out of the operation of this Act, or for the Minister's proper ministerial functions, or of information otherwise available to the public (s 28(3), the text's no)`
`D justified` MEANS `the elements of s 28(1) are met, but the person is not criminally responsible if the disclosure was justified or excused by or under a law (Criminal Code s 43BE, as the note to s 28(3) says); as you state it, it was`
`D yes` MEANS `yes: the elements of the offence in s 28(1) are met (strict liability applies to how the information was obtained, s 28(2)); maximum penalty 200 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years; whether there is a conviction is for a court`
`disclosure` MEANS `s 28 -- was disclosing my information an offence`

-- Inputs: obtained in administering the Act, disclosed, why, already public, justified by another law.
#ASSERT `disclosure` FALSE TRUE `for none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D not obtained`
#ASSERT `disclosure` TRUE FALSE `for none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D none`
#ASSERT `disclosure` TRUE TRUE `for none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D yes`
#ASSERT `disclosure` TRUE TRUE `for none of these` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `D justified`
#ASSERT `disclosure` TRUE TRUE `for the administration of this Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D excepted`
#ASSERT `disclosure` TRUE TRUE `with my consent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D excepted`
#ASSERT `disclosure` TRUE TRUE `for legal proceedings arising out of the operation of this Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D excepted`
#ASSERT `disclosure` TRUE TRUE `for the proper performance of the Minister's ministerial functions and duties` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D excepted`
#ASSERT `disclosure` TRUE TRUE `for none of these` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `D excepted`
-- An excepted disclosure needs no justification under another law; the exception is answered first.
#ASSERT `disclosure` TRUE TRUE `with my consent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `D excepted`

-- The regulative rule on its own: a disclosure outside s 28(3) breaches it; an excepted one and none at all do not.
#ASSERT `s 28 -- the prohibition was kept` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28 -- the prohibition was kept` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28 -- the prohibition was kept` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 28 -- the prohibition was kept` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `excepted by s 28(3)` `for none of these` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`excepted by s 28(3)` `for none of these` FALSE))

-- The maximum fine: 200 penalty units. Penalty unit values below are hypothetical round figures.
#ASSERT `s 28 -- the most I could see them fined` 100 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `s 28 -- the most I could see them fined` 162 EQUALS 32400
#ASSERT `s 28 -- the most I could see them fined` 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 12(3) -- is the sealed document taken as the Commission's`

`S yes` MEANS `yes: a document that purports to bear the Commission's common seal is taken to have been duly executed by the Commission (s 12(3))`
`S evidence` MEANS `this Act does not say: the presumption in s 12(3) gives way to evidence to the contrary, and whether the Commission executed it is then a question of fact (NOTHING-kind)`
`S no seal` MEANS `this Act does not say: s 12(3) speaks only of documents bearing the Commission's common seal (NOTHING-kind)`
`sealed` MEANS `s 12(3) -- is the sealed document taken as the Commission's`

#ASSERT `sealed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `S yes`
#ASSERT `sealed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S evidence`
#ASSERT `sealed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `S no seal`
#ASSERT `sealed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `S no seal`

§ `s 5(1), s 43 -- does what was done with TIO still count`

`T yes` MEANS `yes: it is taken to have been done by, to or in relation to the Commission (s 43(1)), which is TIO continued as the same corporate entity (s 5(1)); if it was done for a provision of the Territory Insurance Office Act 1979, it counts for the equivalent provision of this Act (s 43(2))`
`T spent` MEANS `s 43 does not carry it over, since it was not of ongoing effect (NOTHING-kind); the Commission is still the same corporate entity as TIO (s 5(1))`
`T after` MEANS `no: s 43 covers only what was done before the Act commenced on 1 January 2015 (the text's no); by then TIO was already the Commission, continued as the same corporate entity (s 5(1))`
`tio` MEANS `s 5(1), s 43 -- does what was done with TIO still count`

-- The last day before the commencement, the day of it, and well before.
#ASSERT `tio` (`the calendar date` 31 12 2014) TRUE EQUALS `T yes`
#ASSERT `tio` (`the calendar date` 31 12 2014) FALSE EQUALS `T spent`
#ASSERT `tio` (`the calendar date` 1 1 2015) TRUE EQUALS `T after`
#ASSERT `tio` (`the calendar date` 2 1 2015) FALSE EQUALS `T after`
#ASSERT `tio` (`the calendar date` 15 6 2010) TRUE EQUALS `T yes`
#ASSERT `before the commencement of the Act` (`the calendar date` 31 12 2014)
#ASSERT (NOT (`before the commencement of the Act` (`the calendar date` 1 1 2015)))

§ `s 30, s 33 -- who deals with my old TIO matter`

`O insurance` MEANS `the Commission: it has the function of winding up TIO's residual insurance business, the part not included in the sale (s 30(1), (3)); s 27's guarantee does not cover it (NOTHING-kind)`
`O deposit` MEANS `the Commission: it carries on TIO's residual banking business until all residual deposits have been repaid, and then winds it up (s 33(2)); the moneys of that business are the Territory's property, held by the Commission and used for no other purpose (s 34(1), (2))`
`O sold` MEANS `not this Act: your policy or deposit went with the sale under the Territory Insurance Office (Sale) Act 2014, and this Act does not say who deals with it (NOTHING-kind)`
`old tio` MEANS `s 30, s 33 -- who deals with my old TIO matter`

#ASSERT `old tio` `an insurance policy or claim with TIO` FALSE EQUALS `O insurance`
#ASSERT `old tio` `an insurance policy or claim with TIO` TRUE EQUALS `O sold`
#ASSERT `old tio` `a deposit with TIO` FALSE EQUALS `O deposit`
#ASSERT `old tio` `a deposit with TIO` TRUE EQUALS `O sold`
